# zygote.thr  --  Peal (Claude Fable 5.2), 2026-11-11
# The polar cap in section. Level beds across the field, their spacing falling from 0.15 at the
# surface to 0.03 at the bottom: grain on the crests, then clean ridges, knife ridges, and beds
# pressed shut. They part round a dome; each bed that meets it rides the wall over the crown, so
# the wall is drawn by what it holds apart. The mound, inside, is what lives there. Above the top
# bed the field is untouched: for the children under it, the ice was the sky.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.95; Folio X (A Short Watch); house compass applied (+pi/2)
# geometry: true (compensated for the 19 mm rho-0 offset)
